                <h3 class="postingHeader">Job Description and Duties</h3>
                <p class="postingContent">
                    <span style="font-size: 12pt;">For questions related to the duties of the position, please&nbsp;contact&nbsp;Forester III<strong>&nbsp;</strong>Colby Forrester<strong>&nbsp;</strong>at (707) 459-7454&nbsp;or by email at Colby.Forrester@fire.ca.gov.<span style="text-decoration: underline;"><br style="text-decoration-line: underline;" /><br /></span>This position is located in Willits, CA.</span><p>You will find additional information about the job in the <strong><a href='https://www.CalCareers.ca.gov/CalHrPublic/FileDownload.aspx?aid=25361043&name=PO-199ForesterIILEResourceManagement7-5-2024.pdf' target='_blank'>Duty Statement</a></strong>.</p>
                </p>
            
</div>

            <div id="pnlWorkingConditions">
	
                <h3 class="postingHeader">Working Conditions</h3>
                <p class="postingContent">
                    <p style="font-family: Arial; text-align: left; margin: 0pt 0pt 10pt; line-height: 1.15;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">The incumbent typically is required to perform psychologically stressful and/or physically demanding duties consistent with firefighting, disaster response, and emergency medical response, including working in isolated areas, walking or running on uneven, rough terrain, and remaining on duty 24 hours or longer without a break while performing these duties.</span></p><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="line-height: 16.86px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">May be subject to working nights, weekends or holidays in&nbsp;support of emergency incidents.</span></span>
                </p>
            
</div>
