        <p class="postingContent">
            <p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt 0pt 10pt; line-height: 1.15;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">Please include position # 542-113-1042-002&nbsp;on your STD 678 form.&nbsp;</span></span></p><p><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="line-height: 18.4px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">Candidate&nbsp;may be selected by resume review.<br /></span></span></p><p style="font-size: 11pt; text-align: left; margin: 0pt 0pt 10pt; line-height: 1.15;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><em>Applicants are highly encouraged to complete a recruitment questionnaire, located at:&nbsp;</em><a href="https://www.surveymonkey.com/r/HLYSH8V" style="text-decoration: none;"><em><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><span style="text-decoration-line: underline; text-decoration-color: initial; color: #0000ff;">https://www.surveymonkey.com/r/HLYSH8V<br /><br /> </span></span></em></a></span><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><a href="https://www.surveymonkey.com/r/HLYSH8V" style="font-family: Calibri; text-decoration-line: none;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: Arial;">Pursuant to California Penal Code 4571, any individual interested in seeking employment who may be required to work with inmates at a conservation camp must disclose of any prior felony status up front, so CAL FIRE/CDCR can provide informed consent to a former felon to be on the conservation camp/prison grounds.&nbsp; Any person/employee that has been convicted of a felony and not received written consent is committing a felony.</span></a></span></p>
        </p>
    
